# Keep screen-capture scratch out of the deployment bundle.
#
# These directories hold the individual JPEG frames (and the per-cue TTS cache) that the
# recording scripts in scripts/ produce. They are working files, not application assets,
# and they are numerous: the five that existed when this file was added held ~7,900 files
# between them. Vercel refuses a prebuilt deployment above 15,000 files, and the failure
# is quiet from the outside — `vercel deploy --prebuilt` reports an error, the alias keeps
# pointing at the previous build, and production silently serves stale code. That is
# exactly what happened: a console text change was deployed three times and never went
# live. `.gitignore` did not cover these paths, and `.vercelignore` defaults to it.
docs/.two-modes-tmp
docs/.two-videos-tmp
docs/.live-scenarios-tmp
docs/.scenario-videos-tmp
docs/.screencast-tmp
docs/.two-demos-tmp
docs/.live-web-demo-tmp
docs/.live-whatsapp-tmp
docs/.web-demo-visual-tmp
docs/.web-demo-voice-tmp

# Frame dumps written by the older one-video recorder.
docs/.demo-frames
